        { "text": "$-21$", "why": "Computed $F(a) - F(b)$ instead of $F(b) - F(a)$." },
        { "text": "$-19$", "why": "Added the two substituted values instead of subtracting them." },
        { "text": "$-11$", "why": "Evaluated $(-2)^{3}$ as $8$, losing the sign of the cube." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$\\int_{-2}^{1}\\left(6x^{2} - 2x\\right)dx$\n$= \\left[2x^{3} - x^{2}\\right]_{-2}^{1}$\n$= (2 - 1) - (-16 - 4)$\n$= 1 + 20$\n$= 21$"
