        { "text": "$18$", "why": "Substituted $k$ into the integrand and solved $8k = 144$ instead of using the primitive." },
        { "text": "$36$", "why": "Stopped at $k^{2} = 36$ and gave $k^{2}$ as the answer." },
        { "text": "$-6$", "why": "The negative square root of $36$, which must be rejected because $k > 0$." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$\\int_{0}^{k} 8x\\,dx$\n$= \\left[4x^{2}\\right]_{0}^{k}$\n$= 4k^{2}$\n$4k^{2} = 144$\n$k^{2} = 36$\n$k = 6$, since $k > 0$"
